# INFAIX Study — environment reference
# Copy to `.env` for local development only. Never commit real secrets
# (`.env*` is gitignored; only this `.env.example` is whitelisted).
#
# Production on Cloudflare Workers: set JWT_SECRET as a WRANGLER SECRET, not
# in `.env`:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET        # then paste the value (Linux/macOS)
#   cmd /c "npx.cmd wrangler secret put JWT_SECRET"   # Windows PowerShell
#
# Production FAILS CLOSED without it (see src/lib/auth/jwt.ts) — the app will
# refuse to start rather than sign sessions with the development fallback.
# Use a long random string (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 48`). Changing it
# invalidates all existing sessions (users are simply re-authenticated).
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string